====================================================================================================
§2  THE COUNTER FRONTIER AND THE SPLIT LAW (in-model)
====================================================================================================
conventions: REF = P2 plane, relaunched inputs [E7], quarter-wave per extra level, c = 1/sqrt(12);
             CONS = REF at the P1 plane; PERM = quiet launch, P2, junction-only levels, multiport, c = 0.02
bits removed per decode = K - ceil(log2(K+1)): K=2 -> 0 (half adder), K=3 -> 1 (full adder), K=4 -> 1, K=5 -> 2, K=6 -> 3, K=7 -> 4
 K  N_op P2  N_op P1     REF 4 K    REF 20 K    REF 77 K   REF 300 K    PERM 4 K
 2   2733.7   1916.3   2.106e-12   1.901e-11   1.212e-06   5.479e-03   2.472e-40
 3   2599.8   1277.5   1.302e-05   3.917e-05   5.016e-03   1.476e-01   4.058e-13
 4   1949.9    958.1   1.847e-03   3.508e-03   5.216e-02   3.310e-01   2.396e-06
 5   2225.3    766.5   3.820e-02   5.417e-02   2.164e-01   5.702e-01   7.343e-04
 6   1854.4    638.8   1.054e-01   1.336e-01   3.414e-01   6.680e-01   1.021e-02
 7   1589.5    547.5   1.909e-01   2.267e-01   4.472e-01   7.354e-01   4.155e-02

split law (77 K, quiet launch): per-comparator spacing^2 = (2 N_op/K) eta_in eta_extra eta_fo(K); with the P2 cap it is 2 N_rail eta_fo(K) / K^2 (eta_fo carries the 1/K split, so roughly K^-3)
  K = 2: spacing^2 at N_op = 400:   98.5114 (formula   98.5114); at P2:   673.250 (formula   673.250)
  K = 3: spacing^2 at N_op = 400:   21.5443 (formula   21.5443); at P2:   140.029 (formula   140.029)
  K = 4: spacing^2 at N_op = 400:   12.1306 (formula   12.1306); at P2:    59.133 (formula    59.133)
  K = 8: spacing^2 at N_op = 400:    1.4938 (formula    1.4938); at P2:     5.194 (formula     5.194)

====================================================================================================
§3  HOW TO ENCODE THE TERNARY PRODUCT (in-model)
====================================================================================================
(a) phase-native signed trits + coherent offset arm [E6], quiet launch, rail at P2:
   T =   4 K, K_t = 1: 3 levels on 2 comparators, N_op = 3899.8, p = 5.526e-22  (K_t = 1 sums nothing: one trit in, one trit out)
   T =   4 K, K_t = 2: 5 levels on 4 comparators, N_op = 1949.9, p = 5.434e-04
   compare at   4 K, same quiet conventions: QFA-3 p = 3.462e-07
   T =  77 K, K_t = 1: 3 levels on 2 comparators, N_op = 3899.8, p = 2.213e-11  (K_t = 1 sums nothing: one trit in, one trit out)
   T =  77 K, K_t = 2: 5 levels on 4 comparators, N_op = 1949.9, p = 3.264e-02
   compare at  77 K, same quiet conventions: QFA-3 p = 1.299e-03
(b) dual-rail balanced ternary, popcount first, then 3^j recombination (5 trits span only +-121:
    int8 needs a 6th trit or a requantisation to 243 levels; both counts below are lower bounds):
   5 trits: 10 rail-planes x 26 counters + 127 recombination counters = 387 counters per 32-MAC block
   6 trits: 12 rail-planes x 26 counters + 197 recombination counters = 509 counters per 32-MAC block
(c) two's-complement bit columns, ternary weight as a select: 236 counters, 8 stages, 12-bit final adder -> (b) costs 1.64-2.16x more

