====================================================================================================
§5  THE LANE: 32-wide int8 x ternary block sum as a Wallace tree (in-model)
====================================================================================================
tree: 236 3:2 counters over 8 stages; per column {0: 15, 1: 23, 2: 27, 3: 29, 4: 30, 5: 30, 6: 30, 7: 30, 8: 14, 9: 6, 10: 2, 11: 0}; 12-bit digital ripple adder
tolerance proxy (the model's own tolerance is open): dot-product SNR of the runtime's own Q8_0 quantisation (absmax per 32, ternary weights): K=5120 gauss 44.3 dB, K=17408 gauss 44.6 dB, K=5120 t4 42.8 dB, K=17408 t4 42.7 dB
int8 activation rms under that quantiser: gauss 55.2, t4 46.1 LSB (the first draft's 127/4 = 31.75 understated the signal)
functional tree exact on 20000 random blocks: select = one's complement for w = -1, sign bit inverted, block constants (+n_neg, -32*128) applied in CMOS
measured counter-level occupancy (s=0..3): [0.2293 0.406  0.2838 0.0809] vs Binomial(3,1/2) [0.125 0.375 0.375 0.125]
error model check at per-boundary tail 0.002: MC variance/block 17975.4 (mean +1.747) vs analytic sum of 4^c E[err^2] 18271.3 (ratio 0.984); occupancy p 3.379e-03 vs Binomial p 3.500e-03 (budget conservative by x1.036)
coherent bias over 160 blocks at this inflated rate: 2.64% of the error power (scales with p)

dot-product SNR at K = 5120 (Q8_0-quantised activations, 1/3 zero weights; t4 / gauss), target 41 dB:
